  "version": "0.7.1-beta.3",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.1-beta.2`\n\n### Features\n\n- add an islands window style: the content sat flush under the title bar, and split panes were set apart by lines; under Appearance, Interface, Window style can now be Islands, which runs the title bar's color around the content as the window's ground and floats each pane, and the empty page, on it as a rounded card, with split panes told apart by the gap between them and dividers drawn only when pointed at; over the window blur the ground takes a lighter tint and the cards still come to the set opacity; the style is remembered for the next launch so it starts without the classic layout first, and it syncs with the other settings ([3c182500](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/3c182500da8075ca9bd22a3606c87b6cd7d83a66))\n- add split layout templates: a tab could only be split one pane at a time, and a layout built up that way had to be built again for the next tab; Split Layout… in a tab's or a pane's menu, or a shortcut left unbound, now lays the tab out as one of six built-in layouts or one saved from a split tab, with its sizes; panes the layout adds open copies of the chosen pane, panes it has no room for move out into tabs of their own, and saved layouts sync and can be deleted there or under Appearance, Split panes ([de082cca](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/de082ccac25377b2863251adbb3da166a2f8538d))\n- add settings for how split panes look: each pane of a split tab always showed a header, and every pane looked alike whichever had the keyboard; under Appearance, Split panes, the headers can now be turned off, which marks the pane with the keyboard by a thin accent frame instead, and the panes without the keyboard can fade by 15, 30 or 45 percent, neither while a pane is zoomed; the settings sync with the others ([48d9ecd0](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/48d9ecd002fb5b70e32926b8084f1bea3fc01a6c))\n- let the overflow menu find sessions in split tabs: it searched only the pane each tab of the bar had the focus in, so a session in another pane of a split tab could not be found; now it lists the panes of a split tab under it, a search keeps a tab when it or any of its panes matches and lists the panes that do, and picking a pane, or Enter on one, goes straight to it ([cc949b8e](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/cc949b8e0ba66a94e8ba5d91c7e0bd900c8d1d68))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.1-beta.2...v0.7.1-beta.3](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.1-beta.2...v0.7.1-beta.3)",
